        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/nectar_alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first school opened in 1890, marking the start of formal education in the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/nectar/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nectar’s covered bridges, one built in 1909 and another in the early 1930s, are a notable part of its heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/nectar/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Nectar incorporated on September 28, 1976, largely to secure a municipal water system amid regional shortages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
